	<item>
		<title>Notes from the tide pool — café edition 🌊</title>
		<link>https://tidepoolnotes.wordpress.com/2024/02/10/notes-from-the-tide-pool/</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 10 Feb 2024 08:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[marenv]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://tidepoolnotes.wordpress.com/?p=41</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Low tide at <strong>6:12</strong> this morning, and the pools were <em>full</em> of life.</p>
<blockquote>“Anemones close up when you look at them too long,” Ana said.</blockquote>
<p>Afterwards: a flat white at the café, and a long argument about starfish — “estrella de mar” &amp; “sea star”.</p>
<p><img src="https://example.org/images/pool-overview.jpg" alt="An overview of the pools" /></p>]]></content:encoded>
